Licensing of the spike/ directory
=================================

This directory builds a WebAssembly port of the Haxe compiler. It mixes
licenses because the Haxe compiler itself is GPL-2.0-or-later.

GPL-2.0-or-later (derivative of the Haxe compiler source):
- patches/haxe-5.0.0-preview.1-wasm.diff
  A modification of HaxeFoundation/haxe (tag 5.0.0-preview.1) source
  (src/dune, src/macro/eval/*, libs/extc, libs/pcre2). As a derivative of the
  GPL-2.0-or-later Haxe compiler, this patch is GPL-2.0-or-later.
  Corresponding source = upstream https://github.com/HaxeFoundation/haxe at
  tag 5.0.0-preview.1 + this patch; reproducible via Dockerfile.

Respective upstream licenses (OCaml library modifications, NOT GPL):
- patches/sha1.ml, patches/unsigned.ml, patches/ctypes-*.ml,
  patches/luv-version.ml  -> derived from the `sha` / `integers` / `ctypes` /
  `luv` opam packages; each retains its upstream license (MIT/ISC-style).
- patches/threads-thread.ml, patches/threads-event.ml  -> a pure-OCaml stub of
  the OCaml `threads` library (LGPL-2.1-with-OCaml-linking-exception upstream).

MIT (original work of this project; Copyright (c) 2026 neguse):
- Everything else here: Dockerfile, build.sh, scripts/*, harness/*
  (node-shim.js, run.mjs, pack_fs.mjs, patch_env.mjs, trace_env.mjs, iter.sh,
  run_node.sh), README.md, HANDOFF.md, results/*.
  These drive / build / test the compiler but contain no Haxe compiler source,
  so they are not derivative works of it.

See ../THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md for the licenses of everything compiled into the
produced WebAssembly artifact (OCaml runtime, wasm_of_ocaml, Haxe std, etc.).
